quest","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5902445683","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49326#issuecomment-5902445683","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49326","id":5902445683,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABX9Ascw","user":{"login":"zdd","id":3888596,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4ODg1OTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3888596?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd","html_url":"https://github.com/zdd","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zdd/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T01:46:56Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T01:46:56Z","body":"This is terrible. I can't input anything on the CLI at all. You should fix this problem as soon as possible and give us 100 banked reset!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5902445683/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5940936526","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/49326#issuecomment-5940936526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/49326","id":5940936526,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABYht_Tg","user":{"login":"giodl73-repo","id":235387111,"node_id":"U_kgDODge45w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235387111?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo","html_url":"https://github.com/giodl73-repo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/giodl73-repo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T21:25:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T21:25:26Z","body":"Follow-up from the same Windows 11 / VS Code integrated PowerShell setup (2026-10-01):\n\nThe user tried `codex --no-daemon` and **still saw separate console windows during tool operations**, with titles resembling `git` and package commands. This means `--no-daemon` is not a sufficient workaround on this machine. A later `codex doctor --json` reported CLI `0.156.1` and a stale/unreachable app-server control socket. A process snapshot showed PowerShell children under CLI `codex.exe` processes, but we did not capture the creator of each transient visible window. I therefore cannot attribute every popup to a specific launch site.\n\nI investigated a candidate fix in a side-by-side checkout of official `rust-v0.159.3` (`01fc69f4026735edfdf6789820549727a4867b11`), without replacing the installed CLI. That source uses background launch helpers for several Git/npm/hook paths, but `PowershellParserProcess::spawn` in `codex-rs/shell-command/src/command_safety/powershell_parser.rs` still launches a background PowerShell process without `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` (also tracked in #49760). My local candidate adds this immediately before `command.spawn()`:\n\n```rust\n#[cfg(windows)]\n{\n    use std::os::windows::process::CommandExt;\n    const CREATE_NO_WINDOW: u32 = 0x0800_0000;\n    command.creation_flags(CREATE_NO_WINDOW);\n}\n```\n\nValidation in that isolated checkout:\n\n- Added a Windows regression test that starts a detached parent, invokes the actual parser on `Get-Location`, and verifies the parser has no visible console window.\n- `just test -p codex-shell-command`: **174 passed, 0 skipped**, including that regression.\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli`: succeeded; the side-by-side binary reports `codex-cli 0.159.3`.\n- File-scoped `rustfmt --check` and `git diff --check`: passed. The broad `just fmt` recipe could not complete because its Bazel/Starlark formatter launcher was unavailable on this host.\n\nThis is a **source-level candidate, not a verified end-to-end fix** for the user's popup storm. We have not run a live Codex tool session using the patched binary or established GPT-6.1 Sol access through it. The globally installed CLI remains `0.156.1`.\n\nPlease verify console suppression for the direct CLI shell/Git/package paths as well as the daemon path, and cover the persistent PowerShell parser spawn in the Windows fix. The original mixed-version daemon finding remains valid, but the new `--no-daemon` observation shows that fixing daemon alignment alone does not establish a complete workaround for this setup.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5940936526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]